From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 01:12:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: XAudio2 calls on a destroyed voice do nothing (patch
 0481)

Samurai Warriors 4 DX crashed about six minutes into a stage again, now
in FAudioSourceVoice_GetState on a source voice it had destroyed, while
the mixer read audio data the game had freed. The game keeps calling
voices after DestroyVoice, which did no harm on Windows: Wine left the
FAudio voice dangling, and gave the voice's object to the next voice
made, so a late SubmitSourceBuffer queued its buffer there.

Patch 0481: DestroyVoice forgets the FAudio voice; every call on a
destroyed voice does nothing (getters give zeros), a second DestroyVoice
is ignored, a destroyed send or destination is left out (outputs set to
destroyed voices only are left as they were; creating a voice that
sends only to them fails without a mastering voice), a voice that
failed to be created forgets the FAudio voice FAudio freed, and a
destroyed voice's object is reused only after 64 more were destroyed.

Tested on the PC's Wine with XAudio2 2.9, 64- and 32-bit, against a null
ALSA device: after DestroyVoice, GetState, SubmitSourceBuffer, Start,
the getters, GetEffectParameters, Stop and a second DestroyVoice are
harmless; the next voice is made elsewhere and gets no buffer it wasn't
given, and still plays; 400 voices made and destroyed take 65 objects;
a voice sending only to a destroyed submix is made, and SetOutputVoices
to it does nothing; without a mastering voice either, creating one
fails cleanly. The same program on the earlier DLL queues the destroyed
voice's buffer on the next voice and crashes.
